Nazli is a Research Fellow at Brunel University London. Her expertise areas are product repair,  product longevity, design for behaviour change, and circular product design. Currently, she works in the PISCES project (WP6) that focuses on mitigating plastic waste in Indonesia.

She is researching reusable, refillable, returnable packaging systems as a solution to the plastic packaging waste problem. Previously, she was a post-doc researcher at Linköping University in Sweden for three years. She completed her practice-based PhD at the Royal College of Art in 2017, funded by the Ministry of Economy in Turkey. During her PhD, she explored the possibilities of visible repair using a design-led methodology.

Nazli has been involved in several international and national research projects, funded by Erasmus+, Vinnova, and UKRI. She holds an MSc and BID in Industrial Design and a BA in Sociology from the Middle East Technical University.
